  "merger_description": "Silk Contract Logistics Pty Ltd (**Silk**) proposes to acquire certain limited assets from Toll Transport Pty Ltd (**Toll**) that comprise Toll\u2019s separate bulk logistics (plastics and glass) business (the **Acquisition**). The assets the subject of the Acquisition comprise owned or leased equipment (trailers, prime movers and other equipment such as a reach stacker and pallet inverter), employee contracts, and two customer contracts.\n\nSilk is a wholly owned indirect subsidiary of DP World Australia (Holding) Ltd (**DPW**). Silk provides port logistics and contract logistics services. DPW, through its subsidiary DP World Australia Ltd, operates international container terminals and providers container stevedoring services at the Ports of Melbourne, Botany, Brisbane and Fremantle.\n\nToll, a wholly owned subsidiary of Toll Holdings Pty Limited, operates a bulk logistics business offering specialised services for the transportation of bulk products. Relevant to the Acquisition, Toll\u2019s plastics and glass bulk logistics business provides warehousing, and containerised and loose bulk transportation services to customers in the plastics and glass industries, predominately in Victoria (through the Ports of Melbourne, Botany, Brisbane, and Kembla).\n\nBoth Silk and Toll\u2019s plastics and glass bulk logistics business operate in the supply of bulk containerised logistics services to customers in Australia.",
